{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>וצפית.</b> It would have been fitting for the Ark to be entirely of gold, but because it would be carried on the shoulder, it would be too heavy. And even though we say נושאיו נושא — that was only for a short time, and it is difficult for me: if so, why was Uzzah punished? And this requires investigation. And likewise we find with the golden altar, that the Holy One, blessed be He, commanded to make it of shittim wood and overlay it with gold; and likewise the copper altar — because they were carried on the shoulder, so it would not be heavy on the carriers." "<b>And you shall make upon it a crown of gold.</b> It appears that it is only for ornament, like a crown, and it is a hint to the crown of Torah. And so it implies in Yoma, chapter בא לו: there are three rims — the rim of the Ark, which is for the crown of Torah; the rim of the Table, a sign for the crown of kingship; and the rim of the altar, a hint to the crown of priesthood. The crown of priesthood — Aharon came and took it. The crown of kingship — David came and took it. The crown of Torah is set aside and standing, and whoever wishes to take it, let him come and take it."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:04:06.138188387Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}